# The source the five per-flavour tocs are generated from, and the fallback the
# game reads on any client that does not honour a suffixed name. Edit this one;
# run `python tools/maketocs.py` and the other five follow. tests/validate.py
# fails if they have drifted.
#
# The interface list is ordered with Camelot first on purpose. A client that
# understands a comma-delimited list gets the right answer either way; a parser
# that only reads the first number gets 16001, which is what shipped and is
# known to work on WoW Forever. Forever is the one client anybody here can test,
# so it is the one that must not be the experiment.
## Interface: 16001
## Title: Manners
## Notes: One click to buff back whoever just buffed you, and nearby players missing yours.|n|cffffd100Mage is tested in game; other classes are implemented but unverified.|r
